    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0259" n="937" xml:id="pg937"/>

                <head>Mr. Burlingame to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 41.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 11, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Perceiving in the English papers by the
                    last mail, that numerous steamers now building in England were said to be for
                    the Emperor of China, I felt it to be my duty at once to inquire of Prince Kung
                    what truth there was in these statements.</p>
                <p>He informed me that eight steamers, most of them very small, had been purchased;
                    that these constituted what is called the Osburn Flotilla, and were all that had
                    been, or would be, contracted for.</p>
                <p>These, he said, all left England some time since, and were now expected in
                    China.</p>
                <p>He could not give me their names, but I will ascertain them, and acquaint you by
                    the next mail.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ANSON BURLINGAME.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> H. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Seward</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
